    {
      "id": "Aeiz1172B85FzoE3Mdfyd",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 259.0226237862199,
      "y": 1053.8426513671875,
      "width": 762.4788208007812,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b38",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 447733574,
      "version": 796,
      "versionNonce": 1816075123,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790463506135,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "However, we can think in another way which we see the system as a combination of \n2 Column vectors: #1 and #2 \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "However, we can think in another way which we see the system as a combination of \n2 Column vectors: #1 and #2 \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "L5a7QfnMw0YoiGupMMo9Y",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1303.5216123464882,
      "y": 1034.204764229911,
      "width": 723.89892578125,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b39",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 274485049,
      "version": 1155,
      "versionNonce": 1332267325,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790463506135,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Finding solution Ax = b is equivalent to figure out if vector x will be the same as \nvector b after going through transformation of matrix A",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Finding solution Ax = b is equivalent to figure out if vector x will be the same as \nvector b after going through transformation of matrix A",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "KfljnGnEXqi_f93oHQkKU",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1307.2592309290774,
      "y": 1371.6477399553573,
      "width": 843.6988525390625,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3A",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1958531031,
      "version": 1602,
      "versionNonce": 1330722067,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790463506135,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Transformation means the basic vectors i and j becomes a1 and a2. Originally vector x\nis expressed as linear combination of i and j and so the solution itself is the same combination\nof the new basic vectors after transformation which are a1 and a2",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Transformation means the basic vectors i and j becomes a1 and a2. Originally vector x\nis expressed as linear combination of i and j and so the solution itself is the same combination\nof the new basic vectors after transformation which are a1 and a2",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
