      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3f",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 115841343,
      "version": 281,
      "versionNonce": 1519398717,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790463506135,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "It's used to reorder rows and it's created by first swap rows of Identity Matrix.\nLet's consider swapping 1st and 2nd rows of Identity Matrix and multiply it with \nan arbitrary matrix:",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "It's used to reorder rows and it's created by first swap rows of Identity Matrix.\nLet's consider swapping 1st and 2nd rows of Identity Matrix and multiply it with \nan arbitrary matrix:",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8dwabyo64ltZzt4D5r3ea",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 291.6753655863399,
      "y": 4416.506309528405,
      "width": 776.4189453125,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3g",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1655199807,
      "version": 1105,
      "versionNonce": 2033921811,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790463506135,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Look at 1st row of matrix P, the 1 in 2nd column which means when this row multiply \nwith each column in matrix A, it only extract the 2nd entry. So, the resulting matrix A'\nwill have the 1st row which is the same as 2nd row of matrix A.\n\nIn other words, by just looking at the 1st row of P whose 2nd column is 1.\nWe can quickly figure out the 1st of the resulting will be the 2nd row of matrix A.\n\nApplying the same logic, we can instantly know 2nd row of A' will be 1st row of A\nand 3rd row remain intact.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Look at 1st row of matrix P, the 1 in 2nd column which means when this row multiply \nwith each column in matrix A, it only extract the 2nd entry. So, the resulting matrix A'\nwill have the 1st row which is the same as 2nd row of matrix A.\n\nIn other words, by just looking at the 1st row of P whose 2nd column is 1.\nWe can quickly figure out the 1st of the resulting will be the 2nd row of matrix A.\n\nApplying the same logic, we can instantly know 2nd row of A' will be 1st row of A\nand 3rd row remain intact.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
